#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:614
#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:703
msgid "Opening trial balance"
msgstr "Balanza de comprobación inicial"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:616
msgid ""
"The trial balance is the complete list of accounts with their current "
"balance. It is crucial to input this data into Odoo so that accounts have "
"the correct balances going forward."
msgstr ""
"La balanza de comprobación es la lista completa de cuentas con su saldo "
"actual. Es fundamental introducir estos datos en Odoo para que las cuentas "
"tengan los saldos correctos en adelante."

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:619
msgid ""
"The process of importing an opening trial balance is done in three steps:"
msgstr ""
"El proceso para importar una balanza de comprobación inicial consta de tres "
"pasos:"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:621
msgid ":ref:`Preparing the trial balance <accounting/get_started/prep-tb>`"
msgstr ""
":ref:`Preparar la balanza de comprobación <accounting/get_started/prep-tb>`"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:622
msgid ""
":ref:`Validating the trial balance <accounting/get_started/validate-tb>`"
msgstr ""
":ref:`Validar la balanza de comprobación <accounting/get_started/validate-"
"tb>`"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:623
msgid ":ref:`Importing the trial balance <accounting/get_started/import-tb>`"
msgstr ""
":ref:`Importar la balanza de comprobación <accounting/get_started/import-tb>`"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:628
msgid "Prepare the opening trial balance"
msgstr "Preparar la balanza de comprobación inicial"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:630
msgid ""
"Export the trial balance from your legacy software. The trial balance should "
"be a list of all accounts in the chart of accounts, each with its balance as "
"either a debit or a credit."
msgstr ""
"Exporta la balanza de comprobación de tu software anterior. La balanza de "
"comprobación debe incluir todas las cuentas del plan de cuentas, cada una "
"con su saldo como debe o haber."

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:633
msgid ""
"Prepare the opening trial balance by inserting the information from your "
"legacy software into the journal entry import template available in Odoo. To "
"access the import template for journal entries, go "
"to :menuselection:`Accounting --> Accounting --> Journal Entries`, click "
"the :icon:`fa-cog` (:guilabel:`Actions`) icon, and click :icon:`oi-"
"download` :guilabel:`Import`. Click :icon:`oi-download` :guilabel:`Template "
"for Misc. Operations` to download the template."
msgstr ""
"Prepara el balance de comprobación inicial insertando la información de tu "
"software heredado en la plantilla de importación de asientos contables "
"disponible en Odoo. Para acceder a la plantilla de importación de asientos "
"contables, ve a :menuselection:`Contabilidad --> Contabilidad --> Asientos "
"contables`, haz clic en el icono :icon:`fa-cog` (:guilabel:`Acciones`) y haz "
"clic en :icon:`oi-download` :guilabel:`Importar`. Haz clic en :icon:`oi-"
"download` :guilabel:`Plantilla para operaciones varias` para descargar la "
"plantilla."

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:639
msgid ""
"Insert the data of the trial balance in the template with the following "
"fields:"
msgstr ""
"Introduce los datos de la balanza de comprobación en la plantilla con los "
"siguientes campos:"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:648
msgid ""
"A reference that identifies this journal entry (e.g., `Opening trial "
"balance` or something similar)"
msgstr ""
"Una referencia que identifique este asiento contable (por ejemplo, `Balanza "
"de comprobación inicial` o algo similar)"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:651
msgid "The date of this journal entry"
msgstr "La fecha de este asiento contable"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:653
msgid ""
"The journal this journal entry should exist in. The default miscellaneous "
"journal is recommended."
msgstr ""
"El diario en el que debe existir este asiento contable. Te recomendamos usar "
"el diario predeterminado de operaciones misceláneas."

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:655
#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:700
msgid "Journal Items / Account"
msgstr "Apuntes contables / Cuenta"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:656
msgid "The account code and/or name"
msgstr "El código o nombre de la cuenta"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:657
#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:701
msgid "Journal Items / Debit"
msgstr "Apuntes contables/Débito"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:658
msgid ""
"The debit value of the account in the company's main currency. If the line "
"has a credit, this field should be left blank. Do not enter `0.00` or a "
"negative value."
msgstr ""
"El valor del debe de la cuenta en la moneda principal de la empresa. Si la "
"línea tiene un haber, deja este campo vacío. No introduzcas `0.00` ni un "
"valor negativo."

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:660
#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:702
msgid "Journal Items / Credit"
msgstr "Apuntes contables / Crédito"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:661
msgid ""
"The credit value of the account in the company's main currency. If the line "
"has a debit, this field should be left blank. Do not enter `0.00` or a "
"negative value."
msgstr ""
"El valor del haber de la cuenta en la moneda principal de la empresa. Si la "
"línea tiene un debe, deja este campo vacío. No introduzcas `0.00` ni un "
"valor negativo."

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:663
msgid "Journal Items / Label"
msgstr "Apuntes contables / Etiqueta"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:664
msgid ""
"(Optional) A label that identifies this specific line of the trial balance"
msgstr ""
"(Opcional) Una etiqueta que identifique esta línea específica de la balanza "
"de comprobación"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:667
msgid ""
"The :guilabel:`Reference`, :guilabel:`Date`, and :guilabel:`Journal` columns "
"refer to the entire journal entry. As such, they should only be populated "
"for the first line so that one journal entry is created containing all of "
"the journal items within it."
msgstr ""
"Las columnas :guilabel:`Referencia`, :guilabel:`Fecha` y :guilabel:`Diario` "
"corresponden a todo el asiento contable. Por lo tanto, solo debes "
"completarlas en la primera línea para crear un asiento contable que incluya "
"todos los apuntes contables."

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:670
msgid ""
"Each line should have only one value in either the :guilabel:`Journal "
"Items / Debit` or :guilabel:`Journal Items / Credit` column, and the other "
"column of the line should remain blank. Do not enter `0.00` or a negative "
"value in any column."
msgstr ""
"Cada línea debe tener un solo valor en la columna :guilabel:`Apuntes "
"contables / Débito` o :guilabel:`Apuntes contables / Crédito`, y la otra "
"columna de la línea debe quedar vacía. No introduzcas `0.00` ni un valor "
"negativo en ninguna columna."

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:675
msgid ""
"To identify accounts when not using account codes, replace "
"the :guilabel:`Invoice Lines / Account` field with :guilabel:`Journal "
"Items / Account / External ID` and identify the account by "
"its :ref:`external ID <export_import_data/different-ids>`."
msgstr ""
"Para identificar cuentas cuando no utilices códigos de cuenta, sustituye el "
"campo :guilabel:`Líneas de factura / Cuenta` por :guilabel:`Apuntes "
"contables / Cuenta / ID externo` e identifica la cuenta mediante su :ref:`ID "
"externo <export_import_data/different-ids>`."

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:679
msgid ""
"Edit the opening trial balance spreadsheet, replacing the following accounts "
"with clearing accounts:"
msgstr ""
"Edita la hoja de cálculo de la balanza de comprobación inicial y reemplaza "
"las siguientes cuentas por cuentas de compensación:"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:681
msgid ""
"Accounts Receivable --> AR Clearing (:guilabel:`Type` = :guilabel:`Current "
"Assets`)"
msgstr ""
"Cuentas por cobrar --> Compensación de cuentas por cobrar (:guilabel:`Tipo` "
"= :guilabel:`Activos corrientes`)"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:682
msgid ""
"Accounts Payable --> AP Clearing (:guilabel:`Type` = :guilabel:`Current "
"Assets`)"
msgstr ""
"Cuentas por pagar --> Compensación de cuentas por pagar (:guilabel:`Tipo` "
"= :guilabel:`Activos corrientes`)"

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:686
msgid ""
"In the :ref:`final validation step <accounting/get_started/validation>`, the "
"clearing account types are changed to :guilabel:`Off-Balance Sheet`, so the "
"account type is not critical."
msgstr ""
"En el :ref:`paso final de validación <accounting/get_started/validation>`, "
"los tipos de las cuentas de compensación cambian a :guilabel:`Fuera de "
"balance`, por lo que el tipo de cuenta no es relevante."

#: ../../export/content/applications/finance/accounting/get_started.rst:688
msgid ""
"If you use multiple accounts receivable or multiple accounts payable, they "
"can be merged into a single clearing account."
msgstr ""
"Si usas varias cuentas por cobrar o varias cuentas por pagar, puedes "
"agruparlas en una sola cuenta de compensación."

